1
00:05:03,333 --> 00:05:09,333
A movie about empowering women (the hot ones).

2
00:10:06,666 --> 00:10:12,666
Bottoms is a comedy film directed by Emma Seligman.

3
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:16,000
Unpopular best friends PJ and Josie start a high school
self-defense club to meet girls and lose their virginity.

4
00:20:13,333 --> 00:20:19,333
They soon find themselves in over their heads when the most popular
students start beating each other up in the name of self-defense.

5
00:25:16,666 --> 00:25:22,666
PJ, played by Rachel Sennott.

6
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Josie, played by Ayo Edebiri.

7
00:35:23,333 --> 00:35:29,333
Hazel Callahan, played by Ruby Cruz.

8
00:40:26,666 --> 00:40:32,666
Isabel, played by Havana Rose Liu.

9
00:45:30,000 --> 00:45:36,000
Brittany, played by Kaia Gerber.

10
00:50:33,333 --> 00:50:39,333
Jeff, played by Nicholas Galitzine.

11
00:55:36,666 --> 00:55:42,666
Bottoms is a 2023 American satirical black comedy film directed by
Emma Seligman, who co-wrote it with Rachel Sennott.

12
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:46,000
The film stars Sennott, Ayo Edebiri, Ruby Cruz in her feature film debut, Havana Rose Liu, Kaia
Gerber, Nicholas Galitzine, Miles Fowler, Dagmara Domińczyk, and Marshawn Lynch.

13
01:05:43,333 --> 01:05:49,333
The plot follows two high school senior girls who start a
fight club as a way to hook up with cheerleaders.

14
01:10:46,666 --> 01:10:52,666
Bottoms premiered at South by Southwest on March 11, 2023, and was released in
the United States on August 25, by Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer Pictures.

15
01:15:50,000 --> 01:15:56,000
The film received positive reviews from critics.

16
01:20:53,333 --> 01:20:59,333
The film explores themes of high school, cheerleader,
female friendship, bullying, coming of age.

17
01:25:56,666 --> 01:26:02,666
The tone is lighthearted.
